1 NOTE <b>Cryogladios</b>
2 CONT <p>("Cryo" for ice, symbolizing Grylloblattodea, and "Gladios" for sword or warrior, reflecting Mantophasmatodea's gladiatorial nature.)<b>Myth of Cryogladios:</b>
2 CONT <p>In the primordial epoch of <b>Arthropodica</b>, when the world was divided into realms of eternal frost and endless battlefields, the first <b>Cryogladios</b> arose as a child of extremes. Born from the union of <b>Glaciara</b>, the Frost Que
2 CONC en, and <b>Bellatoris</b>, the Warlord of Storms, Cryogladios embodied both resilience against the harshest cold and an unyielding fighting spirit.<b>The Tale of the Twin Realms:</b>
2 CONT <p>The land of Arthropodica was ruled by two rival forces: the <b>Frozen Expanse</b>, where only the hardiest survived, and the <b>Arena of Eternal Strife</b>, where warriors battled endlessly for supremacy. Cryogladios, caught between these tw
2 CONC o worlds, sought to bring balance.
2 CONT <p>1.</p>
2 CONT <p><b>The Frozen Journey (Grylloblattodea):</b></p>
2 CONT <p>To prove their worth to Glaciara, Cryogladios embarked on the <b>Frozen Journey</b>, traveling deep into the glacial mountains. They faced storms of biting ice and creatures of frost, learning to endure the unrelenting cold. From this, they g
2 CONC ained the ability to survive in the harshest of environments, a trait passed on to their descendants, the <b>Ice Crawlers</b>, who now dwell in icy isolation.
2 CONT <p>2.</p>
2 CONT <p><b>The Trial of Blades (Mantophasmatodea):</b></p>
2 CONT <p>To earn Bellatoris's approval, Cryogladios entered the <b>Arena of Eternal Strife</b>, where they wielded a blade forged from frozen lightning. Facing foes of unmatched skill, they honed their prowess in combat and emerged victorious. This st
2 CONC rength was inherited by the <b>Gladiators</b>, who became masters of strategy and battle.<b>The Clash and the Legacy:</b>
2 CONT <p>Despite their mastery of both worlds, Cryogladios saw the futility of eternal rivalry and sought to unite the realms. They brokered a truce between the Frost Queen and the Warlord of Storms, allowing the two forces to coexist. However, peac
2 CONC e came at a cost: Cryogladios was shattered into two essences, each imbued into their offspring.
2 CONT <p>• From their <b>icy resilience</b>, the <b>Grylloblattodea</b> were born, thriving in frozen, desolate places.
2 CONT <p>• From their <b>martial spirit</b>, the <b>Mantophasmatodea</b> arose, embodying the unyielding strength of warriors.
2 CONT <p>To this day, Cryogladios is remembered as the ancestor who bridged two extremes—cold and combat—leaving behind descendants who reflect their dual legacy of survival and strength.
