2 CONC dows: 2; margin: 0.25em 0px; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 1.6; background-color: #ffffff; text-indent: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-thickness: initial; te
2 CONC xt-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;">
2 CONT <p><h3 id="Internal_relationships" style="font-family: inherit; font-weight: bold; margin: 0px 0px 0.25em; display: inline; line-height: 1.6; font-stretch: inherit; font-optical-sizing: inherit; font-size-adjust: inherit; font-kerning: inherit
2 CONC ; font-feature-settings: inherit; font-variation-settings: inherit; border: 0px; padding: 0px;"><span style="font-size: large;">Internal relationships</span></h3>
2 CONT <p><span class="mw-editsection" style="font-size: small; font-family: sans-serif; vertical-align: baseline; font-weight: normal; margin-left: 1em; line-height: 0; margin-right: 0px; user-select: none; margin-inline: 1em 0px;"><span class="mw-edi
2 CONC tsection-bracket" style="margin-right: 0.25em; margin-inline: 0px 0.25em;"><span style="font-size: medium;">[</span></span><a style="text-decoration: none; background: none transparent scroll repeat 0% 0%; white-space: nowrap; border-radius: 0px
2 CONC ; overflow-wrap: break-word;" title="Edit section: Internal relationships" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Teleost&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4"><span><span style="font-size: medium;">edit</span></span></a><span class="mw-edits
2 CONC ection-bracket" style="margin-left: 0.25em; margin-inline: 0.25em 0px;"><span style="font-size: medium;">]</span></span></span></div>
2 CONT <p><p style="font-size: 16px; font-family: sans-serif; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; font-weight: 400; color: #202122; font-style: normal; orphans: 2; widows: 2; margin: 0.5em 0px 1em; letter-spacing: normal; back
2 CONC ground-color: #ffffff; text-indent: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;">The phylogen
2 CONC y of the teleosts has been subject to long debate, without consensus on either their<span>&nbsp;</span><a style="text-decoration: none; background: none transparent scroll repeat 0% 0%; border-radius: 0px; overflow-wrap: break-word;" title="Phyl
2 CONC ogenetic tree" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phylogenetic_tree">phylogeny</a><span>&nbsp;</span>or the timing of the emergence of the major groups before the application of modern<span>&nbsp;</span><a style="text-decoration: none; backgrou
2 CONC nd: none transparent scroll repeat 0% 0%; border-radius: 0px; overflow-wrap: break-word;" title="DNA" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DNA">DNA</a>-based cladistic analysis. Near et al. (2012) explored the phylogeny and divergence times of ev
2 CONC ery major lineage, analysing the DNA sequences of 9 unlinked genes in 232 species. They obtained well-resolved phylogenies with strong support for the nodes (so, the pattern of branching shown is likely to be correct). They calibrated (set actua
2 CONC l values for) branching times in this tree from 36 reliable measurements of absolute time from the fossil record.<sup id="cite_ref-PNAS_16-3" class="reference" style="font-size: 12px; white-space: nowrap; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal
2 CONC ; line-height: 1;"><a style="text-decoration: none; background: none transparent scroll repeat 0% 0%; border-radius: 0px; overflow-wrap: break-word;" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teleost#cite_note-PNAS-16"><span class="cite-bracket" style
2 CONC ="pointer-events: none;">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" style="pointer-events: none;">]</span></a></sup><span>&nbsp;</span>The teleosts are divided into the major clades shown on the cladogram,<sup id="cite_ref-20" class="reference" style=
2 CONC "font-size: 12px; white-space: nowrap; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; line-height: 1;"><a style="text-decoration: none; background: none transparent scroll repeat 0% 0%; border-radius: 0px; overflow-wrap: break-word;" href="https://en.
2 CONC wikipedia.org/wiki/Teleost#cite_note-20"><span class="cite-bracket" style="pointer-events: none;">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" style="pointer-events: none;">]</span></a></sup><span>&nbsp;</span>with dates, following Near et al.<sup id="c
2 CONC ite_ref-PNAS_16-4" class="reference" style="font-size: 12px; white-space: nowrap; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; line-height: 1;"><a style="text-decoration: none; background: none transparent scroll repeat 0% 0%; border-radius: 0px; ov
2 CONC erflow-wrap: break-word;" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teleost#cite_note-PNAS-16"><span class="cite-bracket" style="pointer-events: none;">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" style="pointer-events: none;">]</span></a></sup><span>&nbsp;</
2 CONC span>More recent research divide the teleosts into two major groups: Eloposteoglossocephala (Elopomorpha + Osteoglossomorpha) and Clupeocephala (the rest of the teleosts).<sup id="cite_ref-21" class="reference" style="font-size: 12px; white-spac
2 CONC e: nowrap; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; line-height: 1;"><a style="text-decoration: none; background: none transparent scroll repeat 0% 0%; border-radius: 0px; overflow-wrap: break-word;" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teleost#c
2 CONC ite_note-21"><span class="cite-bracket" style="pointer-events: none;">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" style="pointer-events: none;">]</span></a></sup><sup id="cite_ref-22" class="reference" style="font-size: 12px; white-space: nowrap; font-
2 CONC weight: normal; font-style: normal; line-height: 1;"><a style="text-decoration: none; background: none transparent scroll repeat 0% 0%; border-radius: 0px; overflow-wrap: break-word;" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teleost#cite_note-22"><sp
2 CONC an class="cite-bracket" style="pointer-events: none;">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" style="pointer-events: none;">]</span></a></sup></p>
