1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to Hindu scripture, '''Vasudeva''' (Devanagari वसुदेव, IAST Vasudeva), also called Ānakadundubhii ("Drum", after the sound of drums heard at the time of his birth),[1][2] is the father of the Hindu deities Krishna, Bala
2 CONC rama and Subhadra. He was king of the Vrishnis and a Yadava prince.[3] He was the son of the Yadava king Shurasena. His sister Kunti was married to Pandu. Kunti plays a big role later in the war Mahabharata.
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>===Family</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>*Parents: Shurasena (father), Marisha (mother)</p>
2 CONT <p>*Spouse	Rohini Devi, Devaki</p>
2 CONT <p>*Children	Balarama, Krishna and Subhadra</p>
2 CONT <p>*Dynasty	Yadava</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Vasudeva was the father of Lord Krishna. Devaki , daughter of the Yadava chieftain Ugrasena and sister of Kamsa was his mother. Please note that Krishna's father was called Vasudeva (with Va pronounced as V-uh). Krishna was called Vasudev
2 CONC a ( with Va pronounced as Vaa) , which indicated his father's name (Vaasudeva means "of Vasudeva" per Sanskrit rules).May 17, 2015
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vasudeva</p>
