1 NOTE {geni:about_me}
2 CONT <p>Vichitravirya (Sanskrit: विचित्रवीर्य, vicitravīrya) was a king in Indian Religious Texts. In the Mahabharata he was the younger son of queen Satyavati and king Shantanu and grandfather of the Pandavas and Kauravas.</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>----</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>BEFORE HE ATTAINED TO MAJARITY, CHITRANGADA, HAD BEEN SLAIN BY THE GANDHARVAS.</p>
2 CONT <p>--------------------</p>
2 CONT <p>As the name suggests(vichitra = strangeness), so not sure if he was weak or eunuch or homosexual.  So, general perception was that he can't get a wife.</p>
