1 FAMC @F8175@
1 FAMS @F8167@
1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT <p>http://www.american-pictures.com/genealogy/persons/per04840.htm#0</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>RULER OF THE EASTERN PART OF THE EMPIRE 188/7 BC-181/0 BC; d. 181/0 BC</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>{geni:about_me} '''</p>
2 CONT <p>=Brihadratha Maurya=</p>
2 CONT <p>'''</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Brihadratha Maurya (Sanskrit; IAST: Bṛhadratha Maurya) was the last ruler of the Maurya Empire. He ruled from c. 187-185 BC. He was killed by his general, Pushyamitra Shunga, who went on to establish the Shunga Empire.</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>'''Reign'''</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Mauryan territories, centred on the capital of Pataliputra, had shrunk considerably from the time of Ashoka when Brihadratha came to the throne.</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>'''Invasion of Demetrius I'''</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>In 180 BC, northwestern India (parts of modern day Afghanistan and Pakistan) were attacked by the Greco-Bactrian king Demetrius. He established his rule in the Kabul Valley and parts of the Punjab region. The Yuga Purana says that the Yavan
2 CONC a army led by King Dharmamita (Demetrius) invaded the Mauryan territories during Brihadratha's reign and after occupying Panchala region and the cities of Saket and Mathura, they finally captured Pataliputra. But soon they had to leave for Bactr
2 CONC ia to fight a fierce battle (probably between Eucratides I and Demetrius).
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>'''Usurpation of power by Pushyamitra Shunga'''</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>He was killed in 185 BC and power usurped by his general, Pushyamitra Shunga, who then took over the throne and established the Shunga Empire. Bāṇabhaṭṭa's Harshacharita says that Pushyamitra, while parading the entire Mauryan army before Bri
2 CONC hadratha on the pretext of showing him the strength of the army, crushed his master.
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>'''Source : '''</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p># https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brihadratha_Maurya</p>
2 CONT <p># http://www.historyfiles.co.uk/KingListsFarEast/IndiaStates.htm</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>RESEARCH NOTES:</p>
2 CONT <p>King of Maurya Empire; Ruled Eastern part 188-181 BCE</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>-- MERGED NOTE ------------</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>RULER OF THE EASTERN PART OF THE EMPIRE 188/7 BC-181/0 BC; d. 181/0 BC</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>{geni:about_me} '''</p>
2 CONT <p>=Brihadratha Maurya=</p>
2 CONT <p>'''</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Brihadratha Maurya (Sanskrit; IAST: Bṛhadratha Maurya) was the last ruler of the Maurya Empire. He ruled from c. 187-185 BC. He was killed by his general, Pushyamitra Shunga, who went on to establish the Shunga Empire.</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>'''Reign'''</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Mauryan territories, centred on the capital of Pataliputra, had shrunk considerably from the time of Ashoka when Brihadratha came to the throne.</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>'''Invasion of Demetrius I'''</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>In 180 BC, northwestern India (parts of modern day Afghanistan and Pakistan) were attacked by the Greco-Bactrian king Demetrius. He established his rule in the Kabul Valley and parts of the Punjab region. The Yuga Purana says that the Yavan
2 CONC a army led by King Dharmamita (Demetrius) invaded the Mauryan territories during Brihadratha's reign and after occupying Panchala region and the cities of Saket and Mathura, they finally captured Pataliputra. But soon they had to leave for Bactr
2 CONC ia to fight a fierce battle (probably between Eucratides I and Demetrius).
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>'''Usurpation of power by Pushyamitra Shunga'''</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>He was killed in 185 BC and power usurped by his general, Pushyamitra Shunga, who then took over the throne and established the Shunga Empire. Bāṇabhaṭṭa's Harshacharita says that Pushyamitra, while parading the entire Mauryan army before Bri
2 CONC hadratha on the pretext of showing him the strength of the army, crushed his master.
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>'''Source : '''</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p># https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brihadratha_Maurya</p>
2 CONT <p># http://www.historyfiles.co.uk/KingListsFarEast/IndiaStates.htm</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>RESEARCH NOTES:</p>
2 CONT <p>King of Maurya Empire; Ruled Eastern part 188-181 BCE</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>SOURCE NOTES:</p>
2 CONT <p>http://www.american-pictures.com/genealogy/persons/per04840.htm#0</p>
