1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT <p>King of Kashmir and Gandhara</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>VICEROY OF TAXILA; POSSIBLY SAME AS "JALAUKA", KING OF KASHMIR AND GANDHARA
2 CONT <p>(WHO WAS FATHER OF SAMPRATI, RULER OF THE UNITED MAURYA EMPIRE, c. 225/4 BC- c,</p>
2 CONT <p>216/5 BC)</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>SOURCE NOTES:</p>
2 CONT <p>http://www.american-pictures.com/genealogy/persons/per04842.htm#0</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>{geni:about_me} [https://books.google.com/books?id=Tn5oVOER2ogC&pg=PA51&lpg=PA51&dq=Kunala,+King+of+Kashmir+%26+Gandhara&source=bl&ots=MHNXOY4kkZ&sig=jcWmqWneXFMDhNrMVW6v6ADsD3c&hl=en&sa=X&ei=n8HWVI6kIoWigwTLwIDQCQ&ved=0CCoQ6AEwAjgK#v=onepage
2 CONC &q=Kunala%2C%20King%20of%20Kashmir%20%26%20Gandhara&f=false   '''Kinnaur in the Himalayas]: Mythology to Modernity, By Shiva Chandra Bajpai
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Lord Garbhodakasayi (Sahasra-sira Purusa) VISHNU, from whose navel sprang a lotus, from which came Lord Brahmā</p>
2 CONT <p>Lord Brahmā</p>
2 CONT <p>Marici (generated from the mind of Lord Brahmā) = Kala</p>
2 CONT <p>Kasyapa = Aditi, daughter of Prajapati Daksha (son of Lord Brahmā) & Prasuti</p>
2 CONT <p>Vaivasvata Manu</p>
2 CONT <p>Mahārāja Ikshvaku, 1st King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Kikshi</p>
2 CONT <p>Vikukshi</p>
2 CONT <p>Baana</p>
2 CONT <p>Anaranya</p>
2 CONT <p>Pruthu</p>
2 CONT <p>Trishanku</p>
2 CONT <p>Dhundumaara</p>
2 CONT <p>Yuvanaashva</p>
2 CONT <p>Mandhaata</p>
2 CONT <p>Susandhi</p>
2 CONT <p>Dhruvasandhi</p>
2 CONT <p>Bharata</p>
2 CONT <p>Asita</p>
2 CONT <p>Sagara, whose mother was poisoned</p>
2 CONT <p>Asamanja</p>
2 CONT <p>Amshuman</p>
2 CONT <p>Diliipa</p>
2 CONT <p>Bhageeratha</p>
2 CONT <p>Kakutstha</p>
2 CONT <p>Raghu</p>
2 CONT <p>Pravriddha (Kalmashapaada)</p>
2 CONT <p>Shankana</p>
2 CONT <p>Sudarshana</p>
2 CONT <p>Agnivarsna</p>
2 CONT <p>Shiigraga</p>
2 CONT <p>Maru</p>
2 CONT <p>Prashushruka</p>
2 CONT <p>Ambariisha</p>
2 CONT <p>Nahusha, the emperor</p>
2 CONT <p>Yayaati</p>
2 CONT <p>Naabhaaga</p>
2 CONT <p>Aja</p>
2 CONT <p>Daśaratha</p>
2 CONT <p>Lord Śrī Rāmacandra (Rāma)  = Sita, daughter of Bhumidevi; adopted by King Janaka</p>
2 CONT <p>Kusa (Kusha), King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Atithia, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Nisadha, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Nala, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Nabhas, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Pundarika, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Ksemadhrtvan, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Devanika, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Ahinaga, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Pariyatra, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Danu, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Nalavajranabha, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Urnanabha, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Srnkhala, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Vyusitasva, King of Kosala = Princess Bhadra, dau. King Kaksivant</p>
2 CONT <p>Visvasaha, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Hiranyanabha, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Pusya, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Dhruvasandhi, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Sudrasena, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Agnivarna, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Sighrasva, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Maru, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Prasusruta, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Susandhi, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Amarsa, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Shasvant, King of Kosala = Vasundhara Paurava</p>
2 CONT <p>Visrutavant, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Prince of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Brhatksaya, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Uruksaya, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Prince of Kosala, son of Uruksaya</p>
2 CONT <p>Prativyoma, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Divakara, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Brhadasva, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Bhanuratha, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Pratitasva, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Supratita, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Marudeva, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Kinnarasva, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Suparna, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Sumitra [I] Amitrajit, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Bharadvaja, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Dharma, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Krtanjaya, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Rananjaya, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Jaya-Sena, King of Kosala</p>
2 CONT <p>Prince Haryanka</p>
2 CONT <p>Bhattiya, King of Magadha (the usurper) = dau. King Vishvajati of Magadha</p>
2 CONT <p>Bimbisara, King of Magadha (544-491 BCE) = Chellena Licchavi</p>
2 CONT <p>Ajatasatru Kunika, King of Magadha = Princess Vajra of Kosala, dau. King Prasenajit</p>
2 CONT <p>Nandivardha Anuruddha, King of Magadha = Bhadda, dau. King of Bengal</p>
2 CONT <p>Nagadashoka, King of Magadha</p>
2 CONT <p>Sisunaga, King of Magadha</p>
2 CONT <p>Kalasoka Kakavara, King of Magadha</p>
2 CONT <p>Ksemadharma, King of Magadha = dau. Gopaditya Gonandiya of Kashmir</p>
2 CONT <p>Dhananada [Xandrames], King of Magadha = sister of Dhana Nanda of Magadha</p>
2 CONT <p>Nandini  = Chandragupta Maurya [Sandrakottes], Mahārāja of India (324-301 BCE)</p>
2 CONT <p>Princess Subhadrangi Dharmi = Bindusar/Vindusara, Mahārāja of India (301-269 BCE)</p>
2 CONT <p>Ashoka “the Great”, Devanampiya Piyadassi (304-232 BCE) = Tissarakkha Karuvaki</p>
2 CONT <p>Kunala, King of Kashmir = dau. King Devapala of Nepal & a Tibetan princess</p>
2 CONT <p>Brihadratha [II], Mahārāja of India (187-181 BCE) = Princess Berenice of Bactria</p>
2 CONT <p>Princess Sundari of India = King Demetrius of Bactria (200-185 BCE)</p>
2 CONT <p>Princess Alexandra of Bactria = King Agathocles of Bactria (165-160 BCE)</p>
2 CONT <p>Princess Agathoclea of Bactria = Menander I (Soter), King of Bactria (155-150 BCE)</p>
2 CONT <p>Strato I, King of Bactria = sister of Vasumitra, Mahārāja of India</p>
2 CONT <p>Apollodotus II, King of Bactria</p>
2 CONT <p>Hipposatos, King of Bactria</p>
2 CONT <p>Telephus, King of Bactria</p>
2 CONT <p>Princess Calliope of Bactria = King Hermaeus of Bactria</p>
2 CONT <p>Princess of Bactria = Kuyula Kadphises [Kilu-dzilu-kiak], King of the Kushans</p>
2 CONT <p>Vima Kadphises of the Kushans = granddaughter of Susaramana, Mahārāja of India</p>
2 CONT <p>Kanishka I (Devaputra), King of the Kushans</p>
2 CONT <p>Huvishka I, King of the Kushans (130-150 CE) = dau. of Nahapa, King of the Sakyae</p>
2 CONT <p>Vasudeva I, King of the Kushans (150-160 CE)</p>
2 CONT <p>Kanishka III, King of the Kushans</p>
2 CONT <p>Vasudeva II [Po T’iao], King of the Kushans</p>
2 CONT <p>Vasudeva III, King of the Kushans</p>
2 CONT <p>Vasudeva, King of Kabul</p>
2 CONT <p>Princess Ifra Hormiz of the Kushan = Hormizd II Sásání, Sháh of Persia</p>
2 CONT <p>Shápúr II, Sásání, Sháh of Persia = Princess Sithil-Horak of the Scyths & Parthians</p>
2 CONT <p>Shápúr III, Sásání, Sháh of Persia = Princess Tihe-He of Shan-Shan</p>
2 CONT <p>Yazdegerd I Sásání, Sháh of Persia</p>
2 CONT <p>Bahram V Sásání, Sháh of Persia = Sapinud, dau. Emperor Kumaragupta (415-455)</p>
2 CONT <p>Yazdegerd II Sásání, Sháh of Persia = Princess Dhanakha [Dinak] the Hephthalite</p>
2 CONT <p>Peroz (Firuz) Sásání, Sháh of Persia = Mihrandukht, an Iberian princess</p>
2 CONT <p>Kubad I Sásání, Sháh of Persia = Nevandukht the Hephthalite</p>
2 CONT <p>Khusraw I (the Just) Sásání, Sháh of Persia = Princess Kayen of the Turks</p>
2 CONT <p>Hormizd IV Sásání, Sháh of Persia = daughter of Khurad, King of the Hephthalites</p>
2 CONT <p>Khusraw II (Parvez) Sásání, Sháh of Persia = Princess Sirin of Turkestan</p>
2 CONT <p>Sharíyár Sásání, Sháh of Persia </p>
2 CONT <p>Yazdegerd III, Shah of Persia  =  Maha Talat</p>
2 CONT <p>Princess Shahrbanu of Persia, dau. Yazdegerd III (f2)   =  Husayn ibn ‘Alí Abu-Talib, 3rd Shiite Imám </p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>‘Alí ibn Husayn, Zaynu’l-Ábidín (658-713), 4th Shiite Imám  = Fatimah, dau. of Hasan (2nd Imám)</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Muhammal ibn ‘Alí ibn Husayn, al-Báqir, 5th Shiite Imám (676-743)  = Farwah,  g-g-dau. of Abu Bakr, 1st Sunni Caliph</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Ja‘far ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Alí, as-Sádiq, 6th Shiite Imám (708-765) = Fatima</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Isma’il ibn Ja‘far ibn Muhammad (736-760) brother of ALI AL-URAIDI</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Muhammad ibn Isma’il ibn Ja‘far     </p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Isma’il ibn Ja‘far ibn Muhammad (721-755)  =  </p>
