1 NOTE {geni:about_me} King Puru was a Puranic king and the youngest son of king Yayati and Sharmishtha and one of ancestors of the Pandavas and Kauravas.[1]
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Puru in the Bhagavata Purana In the nineteenth chapter of book nine of the Bhagavata Purana, Puru is described as having four brothers; Yadu, Turvasu, Druhyu and Anu. He exchanges his youth for old age of his father Yayati when Yayati gets cu
2 CONC rsed by Shukracharya.[2] In return Yayati makes him his descendant though he was youngest of all. His son and successor is named as his son was Práchinvat; his son was Pravíra; his son was Manasyu.
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Puru in the Mahabharata In the Mahabharata - Adi Parva, he is said to have inherited his kingdom in the Gangatic plain. He is said to have three mighty heroes as sons by his wife Paushti; Pravira, and Raudraswa. Pravira succeeded Puru and wa
2 CONC s in turn succeeded by his son Manasyu.[3]
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Puru ruled from the centre as a supreme World Emperor or King of Kings. This also showed his supreme power and displays the right of people named Puru.[1][2] His dynasty becomes the Puru vamsha which was later renamed as Kuru Vamsha to whic
2 CONC h Pandavas and Kauravas belong.
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Puru in the Rigveda[edit] Another Puru is mentioned as a king in the Rigveda and as the father of Adityas, married to Aditi, living and ruling over and area of the Saraswati river.[4]</p>
2 CONT <p></p>
2 CONT <p>Puru in Korean Mythology A King Puru is also mentioned in Korean mythology as the son of a heavenly king called Haemosu who ruled the Buyeo kingdom. The Korean King Puru went on to succeed his divine father and ruled in peace and prosperity
2 CONC . There is a story that when he grew old in age without any children, he was led to a large stone by a horse. When the horse began to cry in front of the stone, the king had it moved and found a frog bathed in a golden light. The frog quickly tu
2 CONC rned into a handsome boy, which Puru interpreted as a sign from heaven and made him crown prince.[5]
